{"name":"Hogwash","hex":"#969c68","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hogwash","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Foolish talk or writing; nonsense.","A mixture of solid and liquid food scraps fed to pigs; swill. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hogwash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swill","blocks":[{"text":"Swill is liquid food for animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Pig_swill_auction_poster.jpg/330px-Pig_swill_auction_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swill","wikidata":"Q17048144"},{"title":"Nonsense","blocks":[{"text":"Nonsense is a form of communication, via speech, writing, or any other formal logic system, that lacks any coherent meaning. In ordinary usage, nonsense is sometimes synonymous with absurdity or the ridiculous. Many poets, novelists and songwriters have used nonsense in their works, often creating entire works using it for reasons ranging from pure comic amusement or satire, to illustrating a point about language or reasoning. In the philosophy of language and philosophy of science, nonsense is distinguished from sense or meaningfulness, and attempts have been made to come up with a coherent and consistent method of distinguishing sense from nonsense. It is also an important field of study in cryptography regarding separating a signal from noise."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nonsense","wikidata":"Q600499"},{"title":"Hogwash (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hogwash is an album recorded by The Groundhogs, originally released by United Artists Records in 1972, catalogue number UAG 29419. The most recent CD reissue is that of 2008 by BGO Records, catalogue number BGOCD787."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/The_Groundhogs_-_Hogwash.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"